    "land.sub": "Croppers and oases around your village: where to settle and which oases to raid or clear with your hero. map.sql only lists villages, so you bring the terrain from the in-game map.",
    "land.import": "Import a map area",
    "land.how": "<li>In Travian open the <b>map</b> on the area you care about and <b>zoom all the way out</b> (each request then covers 31×31 tiles; at normal zoom, only 11×9).</li><li>Open your browser tools (<b>F12</b>) → <b>Network</b> tab and type <b>position</b> in the filter.</li><li><b>Hover the mouse over the map</b> (dragging it is not enough: the game only asks for tiles when it shows their tooltip). A <b>position</b> request appears.</li><li>Right-click it → <b>Copy → Copy response</b> and paste it here.</li>",
    "land.add": "Add area",
    "land.file": "Open file (.har)",
    "land.manyTitle": "Several areas at once?",
    "land.many": "<li>With the <b>Network</b> tab open and filtered by <b>position</b>, hover over every area you want. Each new area adds a request.</li><li>Right-click any of them → <b>Copy → Copy all listed as HAR (sanitized)</b>, or <b>Save all as HAR</b>.</li><li>Paste the HAR here or open it with the button. Atalaya reads every response and ignores the rest of the file, which never leaves your browser. Do not share that file with anyone.</li>",
